Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:02:44 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: sun50i-h5-nanopi-neo-plus2: add cpu-supply

The NanoPi NEO Plus2 powers the CPU cores from an MP2143DJ regulator.
A GPIO switches its output between 1.1 V and 1.3 V. The DTS describes
this regulator as vdd_cpux.

Set vdd_cpux as the cpu-supply of cpu0. cpufreq-dt can then scale the
CPU voltage with the frequency. It uses only the OPPs that the
regulator can supply, up to 1008 MHz at 1.3 V.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-neo-plus2.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-neo-plus2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-neo-plus2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-neo-plus2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h5-nanopi-neo-plus2.dts
@@ -109,6 +109,10 @@ &codec {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&cpu0 {
+	cpu-supply = <&vdd_cpux>;
+};
+
 &ehci0 {
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
Armbian

